          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Differential algebraic K-theory is the
            = succeed "-refinement" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeTamme12"}> Bunke-Tamme 12
            ) this is realized effectively as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} tangent (∞,1)-topos
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi SmthMfd
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mo )
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo ←
                          %mi coDisc
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi Γ
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi Disc
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi Π
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H} \coloneqq Sh_\infty\left(SmthMfd, \mathbf{B} \right)
                  \\stackrel{\overset{\Pi}{\longrightarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{Disc}{\leftarrow}}{\stackrel{\overset{\Gamma}{\longrightarrow}}{\underset{coDisc}{\leftarrow}}}}
                  \\mathbf{B}
          %p
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            with values in turn in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+schemes"} arithmetic schemes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
            but over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} base (∞,1)-topos
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msub
                      %mi Sch
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{B}
                  \\coloneqq
                  Sh_\infty\left(Sch_{\mathbb{Z}}\right)
          %p
            of algebraic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
          %p
            This may be regarded as sitting inside the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+E-%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth E-∞-groupoids
          %p
            It is observed in this context that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beilinson+regulator"} Beilinson regulator
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            is naturally understood as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            in this perspective of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeTamme12"}> Bunke-Tamme 12
            ), which helps with studying it.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#absolute_hodge_cohomology Absolute Hodge cohomology
          #HodgeComplexOverComplexNumbers.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Stab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Sch
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^\bullet_{\mathbb{C}} \in Stab(Sh_\infty(Sch_{\mathbb{C}}))
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaves"} abelian sheaves
              (regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+of+spectra"} sheaf of spectra
              under the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+Dold-Kan+correspondence"} stable Dold-Kan correspondence
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+Hodge+cohomology"} absolute Hodge cohomology
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+varieties"} complex varieties
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeTamme12"}> Bunke-Tamme 12, section 3.1
            )
          #HodgeComplexOverIntegers.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo •
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi compl
                      %mo *
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Stab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega^\bullet_{\mathbb{Z}} \coloneqq compl^\ast \Omega^\bullet_{\mathbb{C}} \in Stab(\mathbf{B})
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet_{\mathbb{C}}
              under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi compl
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Sch
                      %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi Sch
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    compl
                    \\coloneqq
                    (-)\times_{\mathbb{Z}}Spec(\mathbb{C})
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Sch_{\mathbb{Z}}\longrightarrow Sch_{\mathbb{C}}
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeTamme12"}> Bunke-Tamme 12, section 3.2
            )
          %p
            There is a resolution of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo •
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Disc
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet_{\mathbb{Z}} \in Stab(\mathbf{B}) \stackrel{Disc}{\hookrightarrow} Stab(\mathbf{H})
            by a sheaf of complexes of differential forms on smooth manifolds tensored with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet_{\mathbb{Z}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^\bullet \in Stab(\mathbf{H})
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeTamme12"}> Bunke-Tamme 12, (47)
            ).
          #CyclesForHodgeComplexOverComplexNumbers.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              While
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo ≃
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet \simeq \Omega^\bullet_{\mathbb{Z}}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{\bullet \geq 0}
              which is no longer in the image of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Disc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Disc
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type"} modal type
          %h3#AlgebraicKTheorySheafOfSpectra Algebraic K-theory sheaf of spectra
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Vect
                    %mi lc
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Vect}_{lc} \in \mathbf{H}
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            which to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi SmthMfd
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mi Sch
                    %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\times S \in SmthMfd \times Sch_{\mathbb{Z}}
            assigns the groupoid of locally free and locally finitely generated
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi pr
                      %mi S
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pr_S^\ast \mathcal{O}_S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            (modules over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
            map
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times S \to S
          %p
            This is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
            object with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi 𝒦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Vect
                    %mi lc
                    %mo ⊕
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K \coloneqq \mathcal{K}(\mathbf{Vect}_{lc}^{\oplus})
          %p
            for the stackification of the objectwise
            = succeed "-construction." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+a+symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} K-theory of a symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
          %p
            This is the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#ThomasonTrobaugh90"} Thomason-Trobaugh 90
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#BunkeTamme12"} Bunke-Tamme 12, section 3.3
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "algebraic%20K-theory#AsTheKTheoryOfAlgebraicVectorBundles"} algebraic K-theory – as the K-theory of algebraic vector bundles
          %h3#RefinedBeilinsoRegulator The refined Beilinson regulator
          %p
            There is a refinement of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beilinson+regulator"} Beilinson regulator
            to a smoothly parameterized version
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{K}
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
          #TheBeilinsonRegulator.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p (…)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi r
                      %mi Beil
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    r^{Beil}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    K
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\Omega^\bullet_{\mathbb{Z}}
          %p
            As a homomorphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+objects"} spectrum objects
            this is (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeTamme12"}> Bunke-Tamme 12, def. 4.26
            ). As a homomorphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            objects, this is (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeTamme13"}> Bunke-Tamme 13, def. 2.18
            ).
          %h3#differential_algebraic_ktheory Differential algebraic K-theory
          %p
            Recall the discussion at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+hexagon"} differential cohomology hexagon
          #HodgeComplexOverComplexNumbers.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              %em Differential algebraic K-theory
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi K
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Stab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat K \coloneqq K \underset{\Omega^\bullet}{\times} \Omega^{\bullet \geq 0}  \in Stab(\mathbf{H})
            %p
              of the inclusion of the non-negative degree truncation of the de Rham resolution of the absolute Hodge complex, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CyclesForHodgeComplexOverComplexNumbers"}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheBeilinsonRegulator"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi K
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mrow
                                %mo •
                                %mo ≥
                                %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi pb
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi r
                                  %mi Beil
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\hat K &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Omega^{\bullet \geq 0}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;(pb)&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    K &amp;\underset{r^{Beil}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \Omega^\bullet
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#BunkeTamme12"}> Bunke-Tamme 12, def. 5.1
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BunkeTamme13"} Bunke-Tamme 13, def. 3.1
          %h2#applications Applications
          %ul
            %li
              differential refinement of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Becker-Gottlieb+transfer"} Becker-Gottlieb transfer
              and its image under
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borel+regulators"} Borel regulators
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfer+index+conjecture"} transfer index conjecture
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form+with+logarithmic+singularities"} differential form with logarithmic singularities
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Differential algebraic K-theory as above is introduced with application to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+regulator"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beilinson+regulators"} Beilinson regulators
            in:
          %ul
            %li#BunkeTamme12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georg+Tamme"} Georg Tamme
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Regulators and cycle maps in higher-dimensional differential algebraic K-theory
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1209.6451"}> arXiv:1209.6451
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2015.08.004"} doi:10.1016/j.aim.2015.08.004
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"} David Gepner
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential function spectra, the differential Becker-Gottlieb transfer, and applications to differential algebraic K-theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1306.0247"} arXiv:1306.0247
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/cdn-1608276327798/memo-269-1316/"} ISBN:978-1-4704-4685-7
            %li#BunkeTamme13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georg+Tamme"} Georg Tamme
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Multiplicative differential algebraic K-theory and applications
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.1421"} arXiv:1311.1421
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/akt.2016.1.227"} doi:10.2140/akt.2016.1.227
          %p
            Relevant references in ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            include
          %ul
            %li#ThomasonTrobaugh90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Thomason"} Robert Thomason
              and Thomas Trobaugh,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Higher algebraic K-theory of schemes and of derived categories
